{"id": "section-body-04323", "title": "Human African Trypanosomiasis (HAT), (Sleeping Sickness)", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Protozoa and Others", "Human African Trypanosomiasis (HAT), (Sleeping Sickness)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04323", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Human African Trypanosomiasis (HAT), (Sleeping Sickness)", "runs": [{"text": "Human"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "African"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Trypanosomiasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(HAT),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Sleeping"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Sickness)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1760"}}, {"id": "body-04324", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Human African Trypanosomiasis (HAT), also known as sleeping sickness, is a vector-borne parasitic disease caused by Trypanosoma brucei parasites, transmitted by tsetse flies (Glossina species). It occurs in two forms: Trypanosoma brucei gambiense (chronic, West and Central Africa) and Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense (acute, East and Southern Africa). The disease is endemic in sub-Saharan Africa and is nearly 100% fatal if untreated.", "runs": [{"text": "Human African Trypanosomiasis (HAT), also known as sleeping sickness, is a vector-borne parasitic disease caused by "}, {"text": "Trypanosoma brucei ", "italic": true}, {"text": "parasites, transmitted by tsetse flies (Glossina species). It occurs in two forms: Trypanosoma brucei gambiense (chronic, West and Central"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Africa) and Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense (acute, East and Southern"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Africa). The disease is endemic in sub-Saharan"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Africa and is nearly 100% fatal if untreated."}]}, {"id": "body-04326", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04327", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Symptoms and signs", "runs": [{"text": "Symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}]}, {"id": "body-04328", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "HAT progresses in two stages: Stage one, No CNS involvement (CSF: ≤5 white blood cells/µL, no trypanosomes) and stage two, CNS involvement (CSF: >5 white blood cells/µL, trypanosomes detected, or elevated protein).", "runs": [{"text": "HAT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "progresses in two stages:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Stage one,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "No CNS involvement"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(CSF:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "≤5 white blood cells/µL,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "no trypanosomes)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and stage two, CNS involvement (CSF: >5 white blood cells/µL, trypanosomes detected, or elevated protein)."}]}, {"id": "body-04330", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Haemolymphatic Stage (Stage 1):", "runs": [{"text": "Haemolymphatic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Stage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Stage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1):"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04331", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Early phase after infection, when parasites multiply in blood and lymphatic system. Symptoms are non-specific, often leading to misdiagnosis", "runs": [{"text": "Early"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "phase"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "when"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parasites"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "multiply"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphatic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "system."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non-specific,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leading to misdiagnosis"}]}, {"id": "body-04332", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Symptoms: Fever (intermittent), Headache, Joint and muscle pain, Fatigue, Swollen lymph nodes (notably Winterbottom’s sign: posterior cervical lymph node enlargement in T.b. gambiense), Skin rash or chancre at bite site (more common in T.b. rhodesiense), Itching and/or Anaemia", "runs": [{"text": "Symptoms: Fever (intermittent), Headache, Joint and muscle pain, Fatigue, Swollen lymph nodes (notably Winterbottom’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sign:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "posterior"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cervical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymph"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "node"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enlargement"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "T.b."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gambiense),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Skin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rash"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chancre"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bite"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "site (more common in T.b. rhodesiense), Itching and/or Anaemia"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1759"}}, {"id": "body-04334", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Meningoencephalitis Stage (Stage 2):", "runs": [{"text": "Meningoencephalitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Stage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Stage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2):"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04335", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Parasites invade the central nervous system (CNS). T.b. rhodesiense progresses rapidly (weeks to months), while T.b. gambiense may take months to years", "runs": [{"text": "Parasites"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "invade"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "central"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nervous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "system"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(CNS)."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "T.b."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rhodesiense"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "progresses"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rapidly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "months),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "while"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "T.b. gambiense may take months to years"}]}, {"id": "body-04336", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Symptoms: Sleep disturbances (daytime sleepiness, nighttime insomnia, hence \"sleeping sickness\"), Confusion, irritability, or personality changes, Tremors, motor weakness, or difficulty walking, Seizures and Coma (if untreated)", "runs": [{"text": "Symptoms: Sleep disturbances (daytime sleepiness, nighttime insomnia, hence \"sleeping sickness\"), Confusion, irritability,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "personality"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "changes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Tremors,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "motor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weakness,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "difficulty"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "walking,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Seizures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Coma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "untreated)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1759"}}, {"id": "body-04337", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case Definitions", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Definitions"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04338", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Suspected Case: Any person living in or visiting an endemic area with:", "runs": [{"text": "Suspected", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "person"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "living"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "visiting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "endemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "area"}, {"text": " "}, {"